# EMERGENCY LANDING (ENGINE OFF) (format 1). The checklist is reproduced as printed in the DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist booklet, Edition 4.1 of 2022-10-05, page 9 (owner decisions 2026-10-23, 2026-10-27, 2026-10-28 and 2026-11-03: the booklet is binding): the heading, every item and action, the comment line On final / before touchdown: and the boxed table Approach speed KIAS as printed. The row marks are the numbers 1 to 15 as the booklet counts them; the table is typed as four boxed comment rows (the heading of the table, then the flap position at the left and the speed at the right). The page is graded on the panel where a control shows the desired state, and the other rows are plain lines the pilot ticks on the checklist sheet, which never reach the grade. Graded steps (the order of the rows does not matter, each row is its own unordered group as in the other booklet files): row 3 Power lever FLIGHT IDLE (FI) is the lever at the idle end (travel 10 percent or less; the panel marks no FI position and the engine is stopped, so this is an instructor-review value; standard); row 4 Engine master OFF (critical); row 9 Fuel valve OFF is the state off of the FUEL selector (critical); row 10 Emergency fuel pump OFF (standard); row 11 Fuel transfer pump OFF is the state off of the FUEL TRANS knob (standard, a confirm step: the pump is off in normal operation and the situation starts with it off, so the row is credited from the first frame while it stays off, uncredited when the pilot switches the pump on and leaves it on, and credited again when switched off; it never counts toward the critical steps that fail a do-nothing run, owner decision R-10 of 2026-11-03); row 12 Doors UNLATCH is the state open of the door release lever (standard); row 14 Flaps T/O or LDG is the flap lever at T/O or LDG (standard); row 15 Electric master OFF (critical). Plain lines: row 1 Gliding speed 94 KIAS (the simulation has no control of the speed, the profile glides at the printed speed), row 2 ATC INFORM (the further actions MAYDAY and PAN PAN PAN stand in the footwell), row 5 Adjustable backrests, row 6 Safety harnesses, row 7 Sun visors, row 8 Keypad, row 13 Landing gear AS REQUIRED (no single right state). The situation text is own wording. The instructor-review values are the start of the pilot's restart attempt (the emergency fuel pump is switched on at the start because the printed engine failure list switches it on in the restart attempt, so row 10 has something to switch off; the fuel transfer pump is off as in normal operation, so no FUEL TRANS message shows at the first frame), the start height, the glide rate and the field sight; the engine is dead from the first frame, as in the 09-02 fixture.
format: 1
id: landing-engine-off
title: LANDING ENGINE OFF
source:
  document: "DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist"
  issue: "Edition 4.1, 2022-10-05"
  section: "Page 9, EMERGENCY LANDING (ENGINE OFF)"
  verified: "2026-11-03"
disclaimer: training-aid
scene: outlanding
briefing:
  situation: "The engine has stopped and cannot be restarted. You are gliding at about 94 knots with the propeller standing still, and an open field lies ahead. You decide to land there. Prepare the aircraft for the landing."
initial:
  controls:
    sw.emerg_fuel_pump: "on"
  quantities:
    # The glide start (instructor-review values): 94 knots, 900 feet per minute down, 1500 feet above the terrain; the start values stand here and in the profile.
    airspeed_kt: 94
    vertical_speed_fpm: -900
    altitude_ft: 2900
    # The engine is dead from the first frame.
    rpm: 0
    load_pct: 0
    oil_pressure_bar: 0
    fuel_flow_gph: 0
    fuel_pressure_bar: 0
# The flight profile (in force from the first second at every level; instructor-review values): the engine is stopped and the glide regime applies at the printed gliding speed.
profile:
  engine_stopped: 1
  glide_speed_kt: 94
  glide_vs_fpm: -900
annunciations[1]: oil_pres
checklist:
  form: table
  heading: EMERGENCY LANDING (ENGINE OFF)
procedure[20]:
  - kind: line
    number: 1
    text: "Gliding speed"
    action: "94 KIAS"
  - kind: line
    number: 2
    text: "ATC"
    action: "INFORM"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_power_lever
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: power_flight_idle
        severity: standard
        number: 3
        text: Power lever
        action: "FLIGHT IDLE (FI)"
        done:
          check: travel
          control: lv.power
          op: lte
          value: 10
  - kind: group
    id: grp_engine_master
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: engine_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: 4
        text: Engine master
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.engine_master
          is: off
  - kind: line
    number: 5
    text: "Adjustable backrests"
    action: "UPRIGHT"
  - kind: line
    number: 6
    text: "Safety harnesses"
    action: "TIGHT"
  - kind: line
    number: 7
    text: "Sun visors"
    action: "STOWED"
  - kind: line
    number: 8
    text: "Keypad"
    action: "STOWED"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_fuel_valve
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: fuel_valve_off
        severity: critical
        number: 9
        text: Fuel valve
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.fuel_valve
          is: off
  - kind: group
    id: grp_emerg_fuel_pump
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: emerg_fuel_pump_off
        severity: standard
        number: 10
        text: Emergency fuel pump
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.emerg_fuel_pump
          is: "off"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_fuel_trans
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: fuel_trans_off
        severity: standard
        confirm: true
        number: 11
        text: Fuel transfer pump
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.fuel_trans
          is: "off"
  - kind: comment
    text: "On final / before touchdown:"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_doors
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: doors_unlatch
        severity: standard
        number: 12
        text: Doors
        action: UNLATCH
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.door_release
          is: open
  - kind: line
    number: 13
    text: "Landing gear"
    action: "AS REQUIRED"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_flaps
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: flaps_landing
        severity: standard
        number: 14
        text: Flaps
        action: "T/O or LDG"
        done:
          check: state_in
          control: lv.flaps
          in[2]: to,ldg
  - kind: comment
    text: "Approach speed KIAS"
    boxed: true
  - kind: comment
    text: "Flaps UP"
    boxed: true
    action: "94"
  - kind: comment
    text: "Flaps T/O"
    boxed: true
    action: "85"
  - kind: comment
    text: "Flaps LDG"
    boxed: true
    action: "77"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_elect_master
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: elect_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: 15
        text: Electric master
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.elect_master
          is: off
forbidden[0]:
# The run completes by itself when the aircraft reaches the terrain height of the field (lint L32); the text is own wording.
finish:
  when:
    check: quantity
    quantity: altitude_ft
    op: lte
    value: 1400
  text: The aircraft reached the field
# The further actions (Phase 7, Phase 9). The roles are instructor-review values, listed in docs/PANEL-REVIEW.md; the decision to land is made, so no flight conduct is offered (lint L28, landing scene). The calls and the passenger briefing can never fail the run; the printed row ATC INFORM stays a checklist row.
further:
  actions[3]:
    - id: atc_mayday
      role: recommended
    - id: atc_pan_pan
      role: optional
    - id: brief_passengers
      role: recommended
  conduct: none
